        "filename": "2046-richtext-fddda0e7cd-A-Thousand-No-s-Poet-in-the-City-poem.pdf",
        "src": "/news-media/2046-richtext-fddda0e7cd-A-Thousand-No-s-Poet-in-the-City-poem.pdf",
        "media_type": "other",
        "caption": "A Thousand No's (Poet in the City poem).pdf",
        "alt": "A Thousand Nos",
        "source_key": "/news/Documents/A Thousand No's (Poet in the City poem).pdf"
      }
    ],
    "body": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Students from ISMC were recently invited to a very special poetry workshop run by London-based Poet in the City and AKU- ISMC. "
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\"We do not know where we are going, but we will make it better Than where we have come from. Hope needs no atlas. A revolution is not an event. It is a birthing. A dance of contradictions, the gushing river of tomorrows.\" From A Thousand Nos - created on 27 September 2019 by Momtaza Mehri, Bahia Shehab and ISMC students."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Facilitated by Hip Hop artist, Shay D (Shay Rafati) with Bahia Shehab and poet chronicler, Momtaza Mehri, the evening was the third in a series of events to mark the the recent publication of Bahia Shehab's book, "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "At the Corner of a Dream A Journey of Revolution and Resistance: The Street Art of Bahia Shehab ",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "published by Ginko in association with AKU-ISMC. "
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The session examined whether art as protest can actually make change and asked: Is poetry in itself a revolutionary act? Students were challenged to consider how and why does creativity manifest in the face of oppression and to think about whether street art has always been a symbol of resistance. Working together, the group used street art, graffiti, performance and poetry to create their own original poem referencing the themes of resistance and power that are at the centre of Bahia Shehab's work. "
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Read the poem: "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A Thousand No's (Poet in the City poem)",
